     "<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; <b>On Behalf Of </b>Marcela Gómez<br><b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, August 16, 2023 7:34 PM<br><b>To:</b> oSCR &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br><b>Subject:</b> [oscr] State space using GIS<u></u><u></u></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Hi,</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I was wondering if it is possible to create the state space in a multi-session study using this formula (for externally GIS)</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">df &lt;-</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">data.frame</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">(X=X,Y=Y)</span><u></u><u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">ss &lt;-</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">list</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">(df)</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I tried it in a single-session study and it worked, but every time I try to use it in a multi-session study an error appears saying that I need to create a state space for EACH session.</span><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"> I can&#39;t find any examples of multi-session studies using this formula so I don&#39;t know how to create one per session. </span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I already created the state space in the multi-session study using this other formula: ss &lt;-</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">make.ssDF</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">(scrFrame, buffer, res). But I wanted to know if it&#39;s possible with the first formula.</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">In case to be possible, can you show me an example for a three session study? all of the session uses the same coordinates (X,Y)</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Thank you so much!</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div></div></div>"
